---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteExtras from '@/components/SiteExtras.astro';
import '@/styles/research-primer.css';
import { withBase } from '@/utils/url';
---
<BaseLayout title="Stochastic Optimization" active="Research">
  <main class="site-shell research-primer-page">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="ui-copy-en">Research primer · 02</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">研究科普 · 02</span></div>
      <h1>Stochastic Optimization</h1>
      <p class="research-primer-lede">
        <span class="ui-copy-en">Stochastic optimization is about choosing actions before uncertainty is fully resolved. The central problem is not predicting the future perfectly, but making decisions that remain good across many possible futures.</span>
        <span class="ui-copy-zh">随机优化研究的是：当未来还没有完全揭晓时，我们该怎样先做决策。核心不是把未来预测得完美，而是让当前决策在许多可能的未来里依然表现良好。</span>
      </p>
      <div class="research-primer-meta">
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">Dynamic programming</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">动态规划</span></span>
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">State design</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">状态设计</span></span>
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">Policy structure</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">策略结构</span></span>
        <span><span class="ui-copy-en">Approximation</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">近似计算</span></span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="primer-flow" aria-label="Stochastic optimization mental model">
      <div class="primer-flow-track" style="--flow-count:5">
        <div class="primer-flow-step"><b>01</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Observe state</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">观察状态</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-flow-step is-focus"><b>02</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Choose action</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">选择行动</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-flow-step"><b>03</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Uncertainty resolves</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">随机性实现</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-flow-step"><b>04</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">State changes</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">状态转移</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-flow-step"><b>05</b><span><span class="ui-copy-en">Repeat</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">继续决策</span></span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="primer-section">
      <div class="primer-section-head">
        <span class="primer-section-index">01</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">The basic idea: decide now, learn later</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">基本直觉：先决策，再看到结果</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">Many operational decisions are made before demand, failures, prices, arrivals, or other random events are known.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">很多运营决策都必须在需求、失效、价格、到达过程等随机因素完全揭晓之前做出。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-prose">
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">Suppose an inventory manager decides how much to order today. Tomorrow's demand is unknown. If the manager orders too little, shortage costs appear; too much creates holding costs. Stochastic optimization formalizes this trade-off by optimizing expected or risk-sensitive performance across uncertain outcomes.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">例如库存管理者今天必须先决定订货量，而明天的需求未知。订少了会缺货，订多了会产生库存成本。随机优化就是把这种权衡写进数学模型，在许多可能的未来结果之间寻找更好的决策。</span></p>
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">The difficult part becomes sharper in sequential problems: today's action changes not only today's cost, but also tomorrow's state and therefore tomorrow's options.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">在序贯问题里，困难更进一步：今天的行动不仅影响今天的成本，还会改变明天的状态，于是也改变了明天还能做什么。</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-concepts">
        <article class="primer-concept"><span>A</span><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">State</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">状态</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">The information retained from the past that is sufficient for making the next decision.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">从过去保留下来、足以支持下一步决策的信息摘要。</span></p></article>
        <article class="primer-concept"><span>B</span><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">Action</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">行动</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">The choice made by the decision maker: order, allocate, schedule, route, accept, reject, and so on.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">决策者真正可以控制的选择，例如订货、分配、排程、路径、接受或拒绝。</span></p></article>
        <article class="primer-concept"><span>C</span><h3><span class="ui-copy-en">Transition</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">状态转移</span></h3><p><span class="ui-copy-en">How the current state and action, together with random events, produce the next state.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">当前状态、行动与随机事件怎样共同生成下一期状态。</span></p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="primer-section">
      <div class="primer-section-head">
        <span class="primer-section-index">02</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">Bellman's idea in one line</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">Bellman 思想的一句话版本</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">A good action balances immediate cost with the value of the future state it creates.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">一个好的行动，要同时考虑眼前成本，以及它所创造的未来状态值不值得。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-equations">
        <div class="primer-equation"><code>V(t,s) = minₐ &#123; current cost + E[next value] &#125;</code><span><span class="ui-copy-en">The value function V summarizes the best achievable future performance from state s.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">价值函数 V 概括了从状态 s 出发，未来能够达到的最佳表现。</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-equation"><code>s' = transition(s, a, ξ)</code><span><span class="ui-copy-en">The next state depends on the current state, action, and random information ξ.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">下一期状态由当前状态 s、行动 a 与随机信息 ξ 共同决定。</span></span></div>
        <div class="primer-equation"><code>policy: s → a</code><span><span class="ui-copy-en">The final object we want is usually a policy: a rule mapping observed states to decisions.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">最终真正想得到的通常是一个策略：看到什么状态，就采取什么行动。</span></span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="primer-section">
      <div class="primer-section-head">
        <span class="primer-section-index">03</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">Why state design matters so much</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">为什么状态设计如此重要？</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">A state that is too small loses relevant information; a state that is too large may be computationally impossible.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">状态太小会丢掉决策所需的信息；状态太大，又可能让计算彻底失去可行性。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-prose">
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">This is one reason I keep returning to state representation in warranty inventory models. If the future failure process depends on the age profile of many product cohorts, the mathematically exact state can become high-dimensional very quickly.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">这也是我在保修库存模型中反复考虑状态表示的原因。如果未来失效取决于许多产品批次的年龄结构，那么“数学上完全精确”的状态维度会迅速膨胀。</span></p>
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">The research question is therefore structural as much as computational: can we prove that some information can be aggregated, compressed, or bounded without changing too much of the decision problem?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">所以真正的问题既是计算问题，也是结构问题：能不能证明某些信息可以聚合、压缩，或者用某种近似表示，而不会过度改变原来的决策问题？</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-question-list">
        <article class="primer-question"><span>Q1</span><div><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">Can the state be compressed?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">状态能不能压缩？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Finding sufficient low-dimensional summaries is often more valuable than using a more powerful optimizer on an unnecessarily large state.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">找到低维且充分的信息摘要，往往比在一个过大的状态上换更强的优化器更重要。</span></p></div></article>
        <article class="primer-question"><span>Q2</span><div><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">What structure does the value function have?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">价值函数有什么结构？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Convexity, monotonicity, submodularity, and threshold behavior can turn a black-box optimization problem into something interpretable.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">凸性、单调性、次模性与阈值结构，能把黑箱式求解转化成更可解释的策略规律。</span></p></div></article>
        <article class="primer-question"><span>Q3</span><div><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">When should we approximate?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">什么时候应该近似？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">Approximate dynamic programming, simulation, regression, or neural value/policy approximators become useful when exact recursion is no longer tractable.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">当精确递推不再可计算时，近似动态规划、仿真、回归或神经网络价值/策略近似才真正进入舞台。</span></p></div></article>
        <article class="primer-question"><span>Q4</span><div><strong><span class="ui-copy-en">How do we know the approximation is safe?</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">近似怎样才算可信？</span></strong><p><span class="ui-copy-en">A useful approximation needs more than good numerical fit; ideally we also understand stability, error propagation, and decision loss.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">有用的近似不能只看拟合误差，还希望理解稳定性、误差怎样沿时间传播，以及最终造成多大的决策损失。</span></p></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="primer-section">
      <div class="primer-section-head">
        <span class="primer-section-index">04</span>
        <div>
          <h2><span class="ui-copy-en">Prediction is not the same as optimization</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">预测和优化不是一回事</span></h2>
          <p><span class="ui-copy-en">A very accurate forecast can still be operationally unimportant if the optimal action hardly changes.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">一个预测即使非常准确，如果它并不会改变最优行动，那么它的运营价值仍然可能很有限。</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-prose">
        <p><span class="ui-copy-en">This distinction matters for data-driven operations. Forecasting asks, “what will happen?” Optimization asks, “what should I do, given what may happen?” The second question depends on costs, constraints, timing, and the shape of the decision problem—not only on predictive accuracy.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">这一区别对数据驱动运营尤其重要。预测问“将会发生什么”；优化问“考虑这些可能发生的事情，我现在应该做什么”。后一个问题还取决于成本、约束、决策时机与策略结构，而不仅仅是预测准确率。</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="primer-related">
        <a href={withBase('/research/inventory-warranty')}><small>01 · Application</small><strong>Inventory & Warranty</strong><span><span class="ui-copy-en">A concrete sequential decision problem with failure-generated demand.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">一个由产品失效生成需求的具体序贯决策场景。</span></span></a>
        <a href={withBase('/research/operations-research')}><small>03 · Wider frame</small><strong>Operations Research</strong><span><span class="ui-copy-en">The broader modelling discipline that contains these methods.</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">包含这些方法、更广义的建模与决策学科。</span></span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="research-primer-back">
      <a href={withBase('/research')}>← <span class="ui-copy-en">Back to Research</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">返回研究主页</span></a>
      <a href={withBase('/notes')}><span class="ui-copy-en">Browse technical notes →</span><span class="ui-copy-zh">继续看技术笔记 →</span></a>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteExtras />
</BaseLayout>
